<p>Note 1:  The Company has not released its full earnings report for the quarter ending September 1996 due to the pending sale of MARTA Technologies, Inc.'s three centralized vehicle emissions testing programs to Envirotest Systems Corp. Negotiations with Envirotest and representatives from each of the three states whose programs are to be transferred are continuing.  The Company anticipates that it could incur a loss from discontinued operations with respect to MARTA, both relating to operations and in connection with the loss from the proposed transaction, aggregating as much as $6.5 million ($.24 per share) for the quarter ending September 30, 1996, and $7.5 million ($.28 per common share) for the nine months ending September 30, 1996.  All such amounts are after related income tax benefits.</p>
<p>Note 2:  Represents a one-time non-cash charge relating to the write-off of acquired in-process research and development in connection with the previously announced acquisition of Signal Science, Incorporated in September 1996.</p>
